List every entry of the contents, in the order it prints them:

- title: the entry's title as the contents prints it, with its number, such as "3 Storage and Retrieval" or "Chapter 3: Storage and Retrieval". Join a title that wraps onto a second line.
- page: the page number that the contents prints beside the entry, exactly as printed, such as "87" or "xiii". It is the book's own page number, never the PDF page in brackets above. Use null where the contents prints none, as a part heading often has.
- level: 1 for the outermost entries, such as parts, or chapters where the book has no parts. 2 for what sits under those, such as chapters under a part or sections under a chapter, and so on.

List the front matter and back matter that the contents names too, such as a preface, an appendix or an index. Leave out the entries of any list of figures or tables.

Where the pages hold no table of contents, answer an empty list of entries.
